    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The acceptance suite is the whole test tree \u2014 **all 45 tests pass, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers entirely.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewrote the assignment. It no longer counts owners per city; instead it sets `customerCode = region + \"-\" + HASH8`, where `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. The telephone is already normalized to E.164 by `ValidateOwnerFields` (the first pipeline step), so the hash matches the returned `telephone`. Dropped the now-unused `OwnerRepository` dependency.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getRegion()` derived getter (postcode range first: NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099; then the city table; else `UNKNOWN`), matching the existing derived-getter idiom (`getMembershipLevel`, `getContactPreference`, `getIdentityKey`). This single derivation now backs both the identity's REGION segment and the locality field, so they always agree.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 pointed `locality` at `owner.getRegion()` and removed the duplicated `deriveLocality` method, moving the locality derivation onto the shared region-and-hash identity. `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and `checkDigit` (`luhn(customerCode)`) already reference `customerCode`, so they automatically flow over the new code; updated the Luhn javadoc example.\n\nThe **create audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) already logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now carries the new code with no change \u2014 confirmed by the audit lines in the test output (`NSW-F06A8EAA`, `VIC-65417272`, `UNKNOWN-\u2026`).\n\nThe database `customer_code` column is a plain string, so no schema migration was needed.",
